# The typed copy of the loop takes lists that are as made. An heir of Array is not: it runs the other copy, for ever. Converted to doubles in front of the loop it would run that copy over doubles, at twice the price, and gain nothing:
# so the conversion stands behind the test of being as made. The products stay whole: the heir keeps int32 storage; the list of its class itself is converted.
